K5a cross-review (queue item F2.3), freebuff chat F2, 2026-11-03.
Subject: commit eb0e65b "K5a: read-only xHCI and USB mass storage with FAT32
mounting under QEMU". Its CI failed at clippy (run 41466123174), so its boot
tests have not run in CI.
Question asked: is any check independent of the driver?

Scratch clone: C:/Users/surya/AppData/Local/Temp/rev-f2/k5 at eb0e65b.
Built there: NOVA_TEST=1 bash scripts/build-disk.sh release (build/nova-selftest.hdd
41,943,040 B). Shared working tree not touched.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
1. The commit does not pass its own CI, and the boot stages never ran

  $ gh run view 41466123174 --json conclusion,headSha,createdAt
  {"conclusion":"failure","createdAt":"2026-11-02T14:52:42Z",
   "headSha":"eb0e65b655f5ec2756a10cb0805cbd585c724d83"}

  $ gh run view 41466123174 --log-failed | grep -E "error(\[|:)"
  error: large size difference between variants
  error: the loop variable `i` is used to index `out`
  error: this operation has no effect
  error: length comparison to zero
